      ******************************************************************
      *  Testsuite : CBTRN01C DAILY TRANSACTION POSTER
      *  Program-under-test : app/cbl/CBTRN01C.cbl
      *
      *  Purpose
      *  -------
      *  Exercise the testable production paragraphs of CBTRN01C --
      *  the CardDemo batch program that opens DALYTRAN, CUSTFILE,
      *  XREFFILE, CARDFILE, ACCTFILE, and TRANFILE, reads the daily
      *  transaction file, looks up cross-reference and account
      *  records, and emits status-display lines.  Twelve TESTCASEs
      *  span the open/get-next/close lifecycle plus the diagnostic
      *  display paragraph:
      *
      *    0000-DALYTRAN-OPEN     lines 252-268; OPEN INPUT;
      *                           success -> APPL-RESULT = 0;
      *                           failure -> APPL-RESULT = 12 +
      *                           PERFORM Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS +
      *                           PERFORM Z-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      *    0100-CUSTFILE-OPEN     lines 271-287; same pattern.
      *    0200-XREFFILE-OPEN     lines 289-305; same pattern.
      *    0300-CARDFILE-OPEN     lines 307-323; same pattern.
      *    0400-ACCTFILE-OPEN     lines 325-341; same pattern.
      *    0500-TRANFILE-OPEN     lines 343-359; same pattern.
      *    1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT lines 202-225; READ INTO record;
      *                           '00' -> APPL-RESULT = 0;
      *                           '10' -> APPL-RESULT = 16 +
      *                           END-OF-DAILY-TRANS-FILE = 'Y';
      *                           other -> APPL-RESULT = 12 +
      *                           PERFORM Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS +
      *                           PERFORM Z-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      *    9000-DALYTRAN-CLOSE    lines 361-377; CLOSE;
      *                           '00' -> APPL-RESULT = 0;
      *                           other -> APPL-RESULT = 12 + abend.
      *    Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS    lines 476-489; formats IO-STATUS
      *                           into 4-byte IO-STATUS-04 via
      *                           ELSE-arm overlay or THEN-arm
      *                           TWO-BYTES-BINARY pack.
      *    Z-ABEND-PROGRAM        lines 469-473; LE abend wrapper
      *                           invoked transitively from every
      *                           error branch above; CALLs
      *                           'CEE3ABD' (mocked per-testcase).
      *
      *  Note on Z-prefix paragraph naming
      *  ---------------------------------
      *  CBTRN01C uses Z-ABEND-PROGRAM and Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS
      *  paragraph names (a convention from the CBT*** transaction-
      *  processing programs in the CardDemo source tree) instead of
      *  the 9999/9910 numbered convention used by CBACT01C-CBACT04C
      *  and CBCUS01C.  The Z-prefix denotes "subroutine" paragraphs
      *  that are PERFORMed transitively from any error pathway.
      *  The semantics are identical to the 9999 convention; only
      *  the paragraph identifiers differ.  This testsuite therefore
      *  uses Z-ABEND-PROGRAM / Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS in its PERFORM
      *  invocations, matching the production code at lines 222,
      *  266, 285, 303, 321, 339, 357, 375, 393, 411, 429, 447,
      *  465, and 469-489.
      *
      *  Note on cobol-check 0.2.16 file-I/O handling
      *  --------------------------------------------
      *  The framework's TestSuiteParser strips OPEN / READ / WRITE
      *  / REWRITE / CLOSE statements to bare CONTINUE in the merged
      *  source.  This means the production file-I/O verbs do NOT
      *  execute at test time; the file-status fields retain
      *  whatever the testcase prelude MOVEd into them.  Each
      *  testcase therefore pre-sets the relevant file status
      *  (DALYTRAN-STATUS, CUSTFILE-STATUS, XREFFILE-STATUS,
      *  CARDFILE-STATUS, ACCTFILE-STATUS, TRANFILE-STATUS) to
      *  drive the production IF / ELSE arms deterministically,
      *  mirroring the canonical convention in CBACT01C.cut TC1-TC8.
      *
      *  Note on lookup paragraphs (2000-LOOKUP-XREF, 3000-READ-
      *  ACCOUNT)
      *  --------------------------------------------------------
      *  These two paragraphs use the COBOL READ ... INVALID KEY ...
      *  NOT INVALID KEY ... END-READ compound statement.  cobol-
      *  check 0.2.16's TestSuiteParser strips the entire compound
      *  statement (verb to END-READ) to a single CONTINUE, which
      *  means neither the INVALID KEY arm nor the NOT INVALID KEY
      *  arm executes deterministically at test time.  This
      *  testsuite therefore does NOT directly test these paragraphs
      *  -- their coverage is left to integration-style tests that
      *  exercise the main-loop end-to-end with mocked READs once
      *  cobol-check adds proper KEY-driven mock support.
      *
      *  External dependencies mocked or stubbed
      *  ---------------------------------------
      *    * MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD' (per-testcase, Local scope)
      *      replaces the IBM Language Environment abend service
      *      with a no-op CONTINUE body so the test process is
      *      not torn down when Z-ABEND-PROGRAM is reached.
      *      cobol-check 0.2.16 binds the mock to the surrounding
      *      TESTCASE so the matching VERIFY clause resolves to
      *      the per-testcase Local mock with the per-testcase
      *      expected count.  The runtime stub at tests/stubs/
      *      CEE3ABD.cbl is pre-compiled by the runner and linked
      *      into the merged binary so any unmocked CALL 'CEE3ABD'
      *      (none in this testsuite) resolves at load time and
      *      GOBACKs without terminating the test process.
      *
      *  Internal CBTRN01C paragraphs (every numbered paragraph and
      *  Z-ABEND-PROGRAM / Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS) are NEVER mocked.
      *  Each TESTCASE exercises a production paragraph LIVE via
      *  PERFORM so every assertion validates side effects of
      *  actual production-code execution (per AAP Section 0.10.1).
      *
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16 MOCK FILE limitation (verified)
      *    The framework does NOT support MOCK FILE directives;
      *    only MOCK CALL / MOCK PARAGRAPH / MOCK SECTION are
      *    implemented in features/testSuiteParser/MockGenerator.
      *    See CBACT01C.cut header for full verification details.
      *    This testsuite therefore uses the CANONICAL pre-set-
      *    WORKING-STORAGE pattern for every file-status-dependent
      *    TESTCASE.
      *
      *  Test categories
      *  ---------------
      *    TC1  - 0000-DALYTRAN-OPEN '00' -> APPL-RESULT 0; no abend
      *    TC2  - 0000-DALYTRAN-OPEN '99' -> APPL-RESULT 12; abend
      *    TC3  - 0100-CUSTFILE-OPEN '00' -> APPL-RESULT 0; no abend
      *    TC4  - 0200-XREFFILE-OPEN '99' -> APPL-RESULT 12; abend
      *    TC5  - 0400-ACCTFILE-OPEN '00' -> APPL-RESULT 0; no abend
      *    TC6  - 0500-TRANFILE-OPEN '99' -> APPL-RESULT 12; abend
      *    TC7  - 1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT '00' -> APPL-RESULT 0;
      *           END-OF-DAILY-TRANS-FILE 'N'
      *    TC8  - 1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT '10' -> APPL-RESULT 16;
      *           END-OF-DAILY-TRANS-FILE flips to 'Y'; no abend
      *    TC9  - 1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT '92' -> APPL-RESULT 12;
      *           abend HAPPENED ONCE
      *    TC10 - 9000-DALYTRAN-CLOSE '00' -> APPL-RESULT 0; no abend
      *    TC11 - 9000-DALYTRAN-CLOSE '99' -> APPL-RESULT 12; abend
      *    TC12 - Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS '23' -> IO-STATUS-04 '0023'
      *
      *  References
      *  ----------
      *    AAP Sections 0.10.1, 0.5.1, 0.7.1, 0.10.2, 0.4.1
      *    app/cbl/CBTRN01C.cbl lines 202-225 (1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT)
      *    app/cbl/CBTRN01C.cbl lines 252-268 (0000-DALYTRAN-OPEN)
      *    app/cbl/CBTRN01C.cbl lines 271-287 (0100-CUSTFILE-OPEN)
      *    app/cbl/CBTRN01C.cbl lines 289-305 (0200-XREFFILE-OPEN)
      *    app/cbl/CBTRN01C.cbl lines 307-323 (0300-CARDFILE-OPEN)
      *    app/cbl/CBTRN01C.cbl lines 325-341 (0400-ACCTFILE-OPEN)
      *    app/cbl/CBTRN01C.cbl lines 343-359 (0500-TRANFILE-OPEN)
      *    app/cbl/CBTRN01C.cbl lines 361-377 (9000-DALYTRAN-CLOSE)
      *    app/cbl/CBTRN01C.cbl lines 469-473 (Z-ABEND-PROGRAM)
      *    app/cbl/CBTRN01C.cbl lines 476-489 (Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS)
      *    tests/stubs/STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy (link-time stub state)
      *    tests/stubs/CEE3ABD.cbl         (LE abend stub)
      *    tests/cobol-check/CBACT01C.cut  (canonical pattern)
      *    tests/cobol-check/CBACT02C.cut  (canonical pattern)
      *    tests/cobol-check/CBCUS01C.cut  (Z-prefix pattern source)
      ******************************************************************

       TESTSUITE 'CBTRN01C DAILY TRANSACTION POSTER'.

      ******************************************************************
      *  BEFORE-EACH -- per-testcase isolation reset
      *
      *  Resets every file-status field, the IO-STATUS buffer, the
      *  IO-STATUS-04 display field, the APPL-RESULT discriminant,
      *  the ABCODE/TIMING abend slots, the END-OF-DAILY-TRANS-FILE
      *  flag, and the WS-MISC-VARIABLES counters.  cobol-check
      *  0.2.16 resets MOCK invocation counters automatically.
      *
      *  Each testcase prelude additionally MOVEs '00', '10', '92',
      *  or '99' into the relevant file-status field to drive the
      *  production IF arm (OPEN/READ/CLOSE are stripped to CONTINUE
      *  so the runtime never assigns this field).
      ******************************************************************
       BEFORE-EACH
            INITIALIZE DALYTRAN-STATUS
            INITIALIZE CUSTFILE-STATUS
            INITIALIZE XREFFILE-STATUS
            INITIALIZE CARDFILE-STATUS
            INITIALIZE ACCTFILE-STATUS
            INITIALIZE TRANFILE-STATUS
            INITIALIZE IO-STATUS
            INITIALIZE IO-STATUS-04
            INITIALIZE APPL-RESULT
            INITIALIZE ABCODE
            INITIALIZE TIMING
            INITIALIZE WS-MISC-VARIABLES
            MOVE 'N'  TO END-OF-DAILY-TRANS-FILE
            MOVE ZERO TO RETURN-CODE
       END-BEFORE.

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC1 -- 0000-DALYTRAN-OPEN success: APPL-RESULT = 0
      *
      *  PERFORMs 0000-DALYTRAN-OPEN with DALYTRAN-STATUS = '00' to
      *  drive the SUCCESS branch:
      *      MOVE 8 TO APPL-RESULT       (line 253, seed)
      *      OPEN INPUT DALYTRAN-FILE    (line 254; stripped to
      *                                  CONTINUE)
      *      IF DALYTRAN-STATUS = '00'   (line 255)
      *          MOVE 0 TO APPL-RESULT   (line 256) <-- success
      *      ELSE
      *          MOVE 12 TO APPL-RESULT  (line 258)
      *      END-IF
      *      IF APPL-AOK CONTINUE        (line 260-261) <-- exits
      *      ELSE PERFORM Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS + PERFORM Z-ABEND
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    0  -- the production literal at line 256; not recomputed.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- SUCCESS branch (CONTINUE at line 261)
      *              does not PERFORM Z-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C 0000-DALYTRAN-OPEN success APPL-RESULT 0'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO DALYTRAN-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 0000-DALYTRAN-OPEN
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 0
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC2 -- 0000-DALYTRAN-OPEN failure: APPL-RESULT = 12, abend
      *
      *  Mirror of TC1 with DALYTRAN-STATUS = '99' to force the
      *  line-255 IF ELSE arm.  Line 258 sets APPL-RESULT to 12;
      *  APPL-AOK evaluates false; the line-265-266 PERFORM
      *  Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS + PERFORM Z-ABEND-PROGRAM run, and
      *  Z-ABEND-PROGRAM CALLs CEE3ABD exactly once.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    12 -- the production literal at line 258; not recomputed.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    HAPPENED ONCE -- failure branch reaches Z-ABEND-PROGRAM
      *              which CALLs CEE3ABD once at line 473.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C 0000-DALYTRAN-OPEN failure APPL-RESULT 12'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '99' TO DALYTRAN-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 0000-DALYTRAN-OPEN
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 12
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC3 -- 0100-CUSTFILE-OPEN success: APPL-RESULT = 0
      *
      *  Mirrors TC1 but for the Customer-File OPEN paragraph
      *  (lines 271-287).  Pre-setting CUSTFILE-STATUS = '00'
      *  drives line 274's IF guard to its THEN branch
      *  (MOVE 0 TO APPL-RESULT at line 275).
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    0  -- the production literal at line 275; not recomputed.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- SUCCESS branch does not abend.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C 0100-CUSTFILE-OPEN success APPL-RESULT 0'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO CUSTFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 0100-CUSTFILE-OPEN
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 0
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC4 -- 0200-XREFFILE-OPEN failure: APPL-RESULT = 12, abend
      *
      *  Mirrors TC2 but for the XREF-FILE OPEN paragraph (lines
      *  289-305).  Pre-setting XREFFILE-STATUS = '99' drives line
      *  292's IF ELSE arm; line 295 sets APPL-RESULT to 12; the
      *  line-302-303 PERFORM Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS + PERFORM Z-ABEND
      *  pathway runs, CALLing CEE3ABD once.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    12 -- the production literal at line 295; not recomputed.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    HAPPENED ONCE -- failure branch reaches Z-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C 0200-XREFFILE-OPEN failure APPL-RESULT 12'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '99' TO XREFFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 0200-XREFFILE-OPEN
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 12
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC5 -- 0400-ACCTFILE-OPEN success: APPL-RESULT = 0
      *
      *  Mirrors TC1/TC3 but for the Account-File OPEN paragraph
      *  (lines 325-341).  Pre-setting ACCTFILE-STATUS = '00'
      *  drives line 328's IF guard to its THEN branch
      *  (MOVE 0 TO APPL-RESULT at line 329).
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    0  -- the production literal at line 329; not recomputed.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- SUCCESS branch does not abend.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C 0400-ACCTFILE-OPEN success APPL-RESULT 0'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO ACCTFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 0400-ACCTFILE-OPEN
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 0
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC6 -- 0500-TRANFILE-OPEN failure: APPL-RESULT = 12, abend
      *
      *  Mirrors TC2/TC4 but for the Transaction-File OPEN paragraph
      *  (lines 343-359).  Pre-setting TRANFILE-STATUS = '99' drives
      *  line 346's IF ELSE arm; line 349 sets APPL-RESULT to 12;
      *  the line-356-357 PERFORM Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS + PERFORM
      *  Z-ABEND-PROGRAM pathway runs, CALLing CEE3ABD once.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    12 -- the production literal at line 349; not recomputed.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    HAPPENED ONCE -- failure branch reaches Z-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C 0500-TRANFILE-OPEN failure APPL-RESULT 12'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '99' TO TRANFILE-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 0500-TRANFILE-OPEN
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 12
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC7 -- 1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT happy: APPL-RESULT = 0
      *
      *  PERFORMs 1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT with DALYTRAN-STATUS = '00'
      *  to drive the SUCCESS branch:
      *      READ DALYTRAN-FILE INTO DALYTRAN-RECORD  (line 203;
      *                                              stripped to
      *                                              CONTINUE)
      *      IF DALYTRAN-STATUS = '00'                 (line 204)
      *          MOVE 0 TO APPL-RESULT                 (line 205) <--
      *      ELSE [IF '10' MOVE 16 ELSE MOVE 12]
      *      IF APPL-AOK CONTINUE (line 213) <-- exits
      *      ELSE [IF APPL-EOF MOVE 'Y' ELSE error path]
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    APPL-RESULT = 0   -- production literal at line 205.
      *    END-OF-DAILY-TRANS-FILE = 'N' -- BEFORE-EACH baseline;
      *                          SUCCESS branch does not execute
      *                          line-217 EOF MOVE.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- SUCCESS branch (CONTINUE at line 214)
      *              does not PERFORM Z-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C 1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT happy APPL-RESULT 0'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO DALYTRAN-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 0
            EXPECT END-OF-DAILY-TRANS-FILE TO BE 'N'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC8 -- 1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT EOF: END-OF-DAILY-TRANS-FILE 'Y'
      *
      *  Mirror of TC7 with DALYTRAN-STATUS = '10' to drive the EOF
      *  branch.  Production line 208 sets APPL-RESULT to 16 (the
      *  88-level VALUE for APPL-EOF declared at line 144).  APPL-AOK
      *  evaluates false; APPL-EOF evaluates true; the line-217
      *  MOVE flips END-OF-DAILY-TRANS-FILE to 'Y'.
      *
      *  Source of expected values
      *    APPL-RESULT = 16  -- production literal at line 208
      *                          (matches APPL-EOF VALUE).
      *    END-OF-DAILY-TRANS-FILE = 'Y' -- production literal at
      *                          line 217.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- EOF branch terminates without invoking
      *              Z-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C 1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT EOF flips Y'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '10' TO DALYTRAN-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 16
            EXPECT END-OF-DAILY-TRANS-FILE TO BE 'Y'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC9 -- 1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT non-EOF error: abend pathway
      *
      *  Mirror of TC7/TC8 with DALYTRAN-STATUS = '92' (GnuCOBOL
      *  "logic error") to drive the fatal-error branch.  Production
      *  line 210 sets APPL-RESULT to 12 (neither APPL-AOK nor
      *  APPL-EOF); both 88-levels evaluate false, and the line-221-
      *  222 PERFORM Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS + PERFORM Z-ABEND-PROGRAM
      *  runs, CALLing CEE3ABD once.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    12 -- the production literal at line 210; not recomputed.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    HAPPENED ONCE -- ERROR branch reaches Z-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C 1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT error APPL-RESULT 12'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '92' TO DALYTRAN-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 1000-DALYTRAN-GET-NEXT
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 12
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC10 -- 9000-DALYTRAN-CLOSE success: APPL-RESULT = 0
      *
      *  PERFORMs 9000-DALYTRAN-CLOSE with DALYTRAN-STATUS = '00'
      *  to drive the SUCCESS branch:
      *      ADD 8 TO ZERO GIVING APPL-RESULT          (line 362)
      *      CLOSE DALYTRAN-FILE                       (line 363;
      *                                                stripped to
      *                                                CONTINUE)
      *      IF DALYTRAN-STATUS = '00'                 (line 364)
      *          MOVE 0 TO APPL-RESULT                 (line 365) <--
      *      ELSE
      *          MOVE 12 TO APPL-RESULT                (line 367)
      *      END-IF
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    0 -- the production literal at line 365; not recomputed.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- SUCCESS branch (CONTINUE at line 370)
      *              does not PERFORM Z-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C 9000-DALYTRAN-CLOSE success APPL-RESULT 0'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '00' TO DALYTRAN-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 9000-DALYTRAN-CLOSE
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 0
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC11 -- 9000-DALYTRAN-CLOSE failure: APPL-RESULT = 12, abend
      *
      *  Mirror of TC10 with DALYTRAN-STATUS = '99' to force the
      *  line-364 IF ELSE arm.  Line 367 sets APPL-RESULT to 12;
      *  APPL-AOK evaluates false; the line-374-375 PERFORM
      *  Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS + PERFORM Z-ABEND-PROGRAM runs,
      *  CALLing CEE3ABD once.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    12 -- the production literal at line 367; not recomputed.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    HAPPENED ONCE -- FAILURE branch reaches Z-ABEND-PROGRAM.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C 9000-DALYTRAN-CLOSE failure APPL-RESULT 12'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '99' TO DALYTRAN-STATUS
            MOVE 7777 TO APPL-RESULT
            PERFORM 9000-DALYTRAN-CLOSE
            EXPECT APPL-RESULT TO BE 12
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' HAPPENED ONCE

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC12 -- Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS formats numeric '23' as '0023'
      *
      *  PERFORMs Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS (CBTRN01C.cbl lines 476-489)
      *  with IO-STATUS = '23' to drive the ELSE arm:
      *      IF IO-STATUS NOT NUMERIC OR IO-STAT1 = '9'  (477-478)
      *          [THEN arm: TWO-BYTES-BINARY pack]
      *      ELSE
      *          MOVE '0000'    TO IO-STATUS-04          (line 485)
      *          MOVE IO-STATUS TO IO-STATUS-04(3:2)     (line 486)
      *          DISPLAY ...
      *      END-IF
      *      EXIT.                                       (line 489)
      *
      *  IO-STATUS = '23' is numeric (NOT NUMERIC false) and
      *  IO-STAT1 = '2' (not '9') so the OR-guard evaluates false
      *  and the ELSE arm executes.  Line 485 MOVEs literal '0000'
      *  into IO-STATUS-04; line 486 reference-modifies positions
      *  3-4 with '23', yielding '0023'.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    '0023' -- the production literal '0000' MOVEd at line
      *              485, with the test-author IO-STATUS = '23'
      *              overlaid at positions 3-4 by the production
      *              reference-modified MOVE at line 486.  Directly
      *              observable from the production MOVEs; the test
      *              does not recompute or paraphrase the formatting.
      *
      *  CEE3ABD verification
      *    NEVER HAPPENED -- Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS contains no CALL
      *              site for CEE3ABD; the abend service must not be
      *              reached from this paragraph.  A regression that
      *              accidentally introduced a `PERFORM Z-ABEND-
      *              PROGRAM` inside this paragraph would be caught
      *              by this verify.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CBTRN01C Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS formats numeric 23'
            MOCK CALL 'CEE3ABD'
                CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            MOVE '23' TO IO-STATUS
            PERFORM Z-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS
            EXPECT IO-STATUS-04 TO BE '0023'
            VERIFY CALL 'CEE3ABD' NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  End of testsuite CBTRN01C DAILY TRANSACTION POSTER
      ******************************************************************
